*9,009 events**.\n3. Spatially selected the countries intersecting those earthquake points (`countries.ISO_A3`) → **45 countries**.\n4. Filtered `gdp` to those 45 countries via `Country Code ↔ ISO_A3` (45 of 266 rows matched).\n5. Computed statistics on the `2020` column.\n\n### Result\n| Statistic | Value (current US$) |\n|---|---|\n| Count | 45 |\n| **Mean** | **11,865.51** |\n| Std. dev. | 15,191.63 |\n| Min | 512.06 |\n| Median | 5,308.16 |\n| Max | 64,317.40 |\n\n### The 45 countries\nIndonesia, Chile, Bolivia, Peru, Argentina, India, China, Ethiopia, Tanzania, Morocco, Nicaragua, Kazakhstan, Tajikistan, Russia, Kyrgyzstan, Tunisia, Romania, Poland, Greece, Iraq, Italy, Iran, Croatia, Dominican Republic, El Salvador, Guatemala, Myanmar, Afghanistan, Bosnia & Herzegovina, Uganda, Ecuador, Colombia, Portugal, United States, Canada, Mexico, Papua New Guinea, Australia, Fiji, Philippines, Japan, Puerto Rico, Solomon Islands, Vanuatu, New Zealand.\n\nThe mean is pulled well above the median by high‑income quake countries (USA, Australia, Canada, Japan, Italy, etc.), which is why the average (~11.9k US$) sits far above the median (~5.3k US$).\n\nNote: \"last 30 days\" was interpreted relative to the latest timestamp available in the dataset (2025‑02‑15), since the data covers a single fixed 30‑day window.", "tool_errors": [["get_unique_values", "Error: Column 'NAME' not found in DataFrame"], ["get_unique_values", "Error: Column 'name' not found in DataFrame"], ["get_unique_values", "Error: Column 'ADMIN' not found in DataFrame"], ["get_unique_values", "Error: Column 'admin' not found in DataFrame"], ["get_unique_values", "Error: Column 'Country' not found in DataFrame"], ["get_unique_values", "Error: Column 'SOVEREIGNT' not found in DataFrame"], ["get_unique_values", "Error: Column 'sovereignt' not found in DataFrame"], ["get_unique_values", "Error: Column 'iso_a3' not found in DataFrame"], ["get_unique_values", "Error: Column 'ADM0_A3' not found in DataFrame"], ["ge